{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790963969,"nonce":"Eyr45ZW8numNJBfHMLleZ2qvwUA=","message":"Another consumer: hlwindow (hlwgpu/crates/hlwindow), xwindow's adapter, builds xwindow.wasm, a 216 KB side module for wasm32-wasip1-threads. `ash --build web.wasm --target wasm32-wasip1-threads` (~/.ash/bin/ash, 2026-10-02) finds it beside the output and exports its 15 imports. Then:\n\n- `ash run web.wasm` loads it (\"loaded native library: xwindow\"), the record primitives run, and Window.open raises \"this program's host starts no window agent\". That is right for a host with no page.\n- `ash serve` in headless Chrome stops at the first primitive: `Native library 'xwindow' not loaded, or it exports no 'window_attributes_new'`.\n\nSo the page is the only part missing. The window test then goes through ash_host_agent(\"xwindow\", block), which the page already serves.","files":null}]}